---
// Exam Prep, the front door: starts from the problems aspirants feel, builds up step by step,
// and only then introduces the two tools. Short Q&A, every answer well under 2 minutes.
// Text rules: docs/VISION.md (no guarantees, no pressure). Guide: docs/14-exam-prep.md
import ExamLayout from '../../layouts/ExamLayout.astro';
import { STATS, CI, GUIDE, fmt } from '../../exam-prep';

const secs = (s: string) => Math.max(15, Math.round((s.split(/\s+/).length / 200) * 60 / 5) * 5);
type QA = { q: string; a: string[] };
const chapters: { kicker: string; title: string; qa: QA[] }[] = [
  {
    kicker: 'Part 1',
    title: 'Does any of this sound like you?',
    qa: [
      {
        q: 'Why does the syllabus feel like a mountain?',
        a: [
          'Because nobody shows you the whole of it at once. You get one book for history, another for polity, a coaching list for Rajasthan GK, and a PDF that a friend forwarded. Each one looks finished on its own, and none of them tells you how big the whole thing is.',
          'When you can\'t see the edges of a task, your mind fills the gap with "it\'s endless". That feeling is not laziness. It is what uncertainty feels like.',
        ],
      },
      {
        q: 'Why do I keep starting, and never finishing?',
        a: [
          'Most of us start at chapter one of the thickest book, because that feels responsible. Three weeks later we are still in ancient history, the exam date has not moved, and we quietly start again with a new book.',
          'The problem is rarely discipline. It is starting without knowing which pages matter most for your exam.',
        ],
      },
      {
        q: 'Why does everyone give different advice?',
        a: [
          'Every topper, teacher and channel remembers their own exam, their own year and their own strengths. Their advice is honest, but it is one person\'s experience. When ten honest people disagree, you end up following none of them, or all of them at once.',
        ],
      },
      {
        q: 'Why does working hard still feel like guessing?',
        a: [
          'Because you are making the most important decision, what to study first, without evidence. The evidence exists: it is sitting in old question papers. It is just too slow to count it by hand, paper after paper, while you are also trying to study.',
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    kicker: 'Part 2',
    title: 'So I tried to fix the two things that hurt most',
    qa: [
      {
        q: 'What if you could see the whole map first?',
        a: [
          `That is the <a href="${CI}/">Exhaustive Curriculum Index</a>: ${STATS.subjects} subjects broken into ${fmt(STATS.majors)} major topics and ${fmt(STATS.topics)} topics in all, in a sensible order, from the basics up. It is big on purpose. Seeing the edges is what makes the mountain stop feeling endless.`,
          'You don\'t read it like a book. You search it, open one subject at a time, and come back whenever you wonder "where does this fit?".',
        ],
      },
      {
        q: 'What if past papers could tell you where to start?',
        a: [
          `That is the <a href="${GUIDE}/">Exam Guide</a>. We machine-read ${STATS.papers} RPSC and RSSB question papers and ${STATS.syllabi} syllabi, and matched ${fmt(STATS.questions)} questions to topics in the index. You pick your exam and how much time you have; it gives you a short list, most-asked topics first, sized to what you can finish.`,
        ],
      },
      {
        q: 'How is that different from a topper\'s list?',
        a: [
          'It shows its working. Next to every topic you see how often it was asked, in which exam and when it was last asked. If you disagree with it, you can see exactly why it said what it said, and decide for yourself.',
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    kicker: 'Part 3',
    title: 'Fair questions to ask before you trust it',
    qa: [
      {
        q: 'Will this guarantee my selection?',
        a: [
          'No, and be careful of anyone who promises that. Past papers show what was asked; they can\'t tell what will be asked next time. What this does is take away the guessing about where to begin, so your hours go into the topics that have mattered most so far.',
        ],
      },
      {
        q: 'What doesn\'t it cover yet?',
        a: [
          'Today it knows RPSC and RSSB best. For SSC, UPSC, Railway, NTA and bank exams it shows the overall pattern for now, because their papers aren\'t added yet. Some exams have only a syllabus and no papers, and a few papers were too large to read. Machine-reading scanned papers also makes mistakes, so treat the ranking as a strong guide, not a verdict.',
        ],
      },
      {
        q: 'Why can\'t I tick topics or log in here?',
        a: [
          'On purpose. This section is view only: nothing you type or pick is saved, sent or tracked, and there are no streaks to make you feel guilty. Keep your progress where you already study, in a notebook or your own sheet. Your list lives in the page address, so you can bookmark it or send it to a friend.',
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
];
let n = 0;
---

<ExamLayout
  title="Exam Prep: see the whole syllabus, then start with what matters"
  description="For RPSC, RSSB and other competitive exams: a complete, searchable curriculum map and a guide that ranks topics by past papers. Free, view only, no login."
  section="home"
>
  <header class="hero">
    <p class="kick">Exam Prep · Curious Sparoows</p>
    <h1>Preparing for a government exam shouldn't feel like drowning.</h1>
    <p class="sub">If the syllabus feels endless, the advice keeps changing and you're not sure what to study first, read on. Each answer below takes less than a minute.</p>
    <ul class="pains" aria-label="Common feelings">
      <li>“Where do I even start?”</li>
      <li>“I've bought five books.”</li>
      <li>“Everyone says something different.”</li>
      <li>“Am I studying the right things?”</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href="#part-1">Read the short version</a>
      <a class="btn ghost light" href={`${GUIDE}/`}>Skip to my exam</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  {chapters.map((c, ci) => (
    <section class="chapter" id={`part-${ci + 1}`}>
      <p class="eyebrow">{c.kicker}</p>
      <h2>{c.title}</h2>
      <ol class="path">
        {c.qa.map((item) => {
          n++;
          return (
            <li class="qa reveal">
              <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">{n}</span>
              <div>
                <h3>{item.q}</h3>
                {item.a.map((p) => <p set:html={p} />)}
                <span class="time">{secs(item.a.join(' '))} sec read</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          );
        })}
      </ol>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="chapter" id="part-4">
    <p class="eyebrow">Part 4</p>
    <h2>Where do I start? Three small steps</h2>
    <div class="tools">
      <a class="tool" href={`${GUIDE}/`}>
        <span class="num">1</span>
        <strong>Open the Exam Guide</strong>
        <span>Pick your exam and your date. Two minutes. You get your list, most important first.</span>
        <span class="go">Find my topics →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="tool" href={`${CI}/`}>
        <span class="num">2</span>
        <strong>Study from the top of your list</strong>
        <span>Every topic opens in the Curriculum Index, with what sits inside it and what it links to.</span>
        <span class="go">Open the index →</span>
      </a>
      <div class="tool">
        <span class="num">3</span>
        <strong>Come back when you're unsure</strong>
        <span>Search any word, even misspelled, to see where it fits. Nothing here needs a login, and nothing is tracked.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sign">One topic at a time, a little every day. आप कर सकते हैं।</p>
    <p class="small muted note">Written by Kritikesh with AI help. The data comes from his Curriculum Index and Exam Guide sheets; corrections are welcome on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</ExamLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative; overflow: hidden; padding: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); border-radius: 26px; color: #f6e7c8;
    background:
      radial-gradient(60% 80% at 100% 0%, rgb(217 150 47 / 0.28), transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(120% 140% at 85% 0%, #2a1f4d 0%, #17132e 60%, #120f24 100%);
  }
  .hero::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; opacity: 0.5;
    background-image: radial-gradient(1px 1px at 20% 30%, #fff8 50%, transparent 51%), radial-gradient(1px 1px at 70% 20%, #fff6 50%, transparent 51%),
      radial-gradient(1.5px 1.5px at 85% 70%, #fff5 50%, transparent 51%), radial-gradient(1px 1px at 40% 80%, #fff5 50%, transparent 51%), radial-gradient(1px 1px at 55% 45%, #fff4 50%, transparent 51%);
  }
  .kick { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e8c584; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.3rem); line-height: 1.12; max-width: 17em; color: #fff3dc; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .sub { font-size: 1.15rem; max-width: 36rem; color: rgb(246 231 200 / 0.85); margin: 0.6rem 0 1.4rem; }
  .pains { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 1.6rem; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .pains li { margin: 0; padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid rgb(242 215 166 / 0.3); background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.05); font: italic 500 1.08rem 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; color: #f2d7a6; }
  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .cta .btn { background: #e8b65a; border-color: #e8b65a; color: #1d1636; }
  .cta .btn.ghost.light { background: transparent; color: #f2d7a6; border-color: rgb(242 215 166 / 0.5); }
  .chapter { margin-top: 3rem; scroll-margin-top: 140px; }
  .chapter > h2 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); margin: 0.2rem 0 1.2rem; max-width: 30rem; }
  .path { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; position: relative; }
  .path::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 17px; top: 8px; bottom: 8px; width: 2px; background: linear-gradient(var(--tree), color-mix(in srgb, var(--tree) 15%, transparent)); }
  .qa { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 36px 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .dot { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: grid; place-items: center; width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--surface); border: 2px solid var(--tree); color: var(--tree); font: 700 0.9rem var(--font-sans); }
  .qa > div { padding: 0.9rem 1.2rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); max-width: 46rem; }
  .qa h3 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .qa p { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .time { font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .tools { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 0.9rem; }
  .tool { display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; align-content: start; padding: 1.2rem; border-radius: 20px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; transition: transform 0.25s, border-color 0.25s, box-shadow 0.25s; }
  a.tool:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); border-color: var(--tree); box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgb(42 35 80 / 0.12); }
  .tool .num { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--tree); color: #fff; font-weight: 700; }
  .tool strong { font: 600 1.15rem var(--font-serif); }
  .tool span { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .tool .go { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .sign { margin: 2rem 0 0.4rem; font: italic 500 1.5rem/1.3 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif; color: var(--tree); }
  .note { max-width: 40rem; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .qa { grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr; gap: 0.7rem; } .dot { width: 28px; height: 28px; font-size: 0.8rem; } .path::before { left: 13px; } .qa > div { padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem; } }
</style>
